# Environment configuration

- Read current declarations in `packages/web/src/vite-env.d.ts`, parsing in `packages/web/src/shared/lib/env.ts`, and examples in `packages/web/.env.example`.
- Keep a single configuration owner per concern: core `env`, branding, analytics, or another existing integration module. Avoid scattered component-level reads.
- `VITE_*` values are public client-bundle configuration, never secrets or user credentials.
- Default API origins do not replace runtime organization/project selection. Preserve `packages/web/src/shared/config/workspace-api-layout.ts` and the transport's target selection.
- Add only variables required by the implemented feature; update the parser/type/example together where relevant. Distinguish build-time flags from runtime capabilities.
